CURRENT BASELINE

Expected post-WO05 state:

- Local Device has canonical filesystem.
- First foreign server has its own canonical filesystem.
- Files and Terminal read the same filesystem truth on each Device.
- RACK-OS exists only while a valid RemoteSession resolves.
- Filesystem currently contains text files only.
- Filesystem is currently read-only.
- Directories are derived from paths.
- There is no generic VFS.
- There is no file transfer operation.
- There is no software package representation.
- There is no installation operation.
- There is no remote execution.
- Existing Processes must remain untouched by file transfer in this slice.


PRODUCT / DOMAIN DECISION

The following distinction becomes explicit:

TEXT FILE
  readable textual content

SOFTWARE PACKAGE FILE
  a transferable filesystem artifact representing a concrete software package

INSTALLED SOFTWARE
  Device-owned functionality
  NOT implemented in this Work Order

RUNNING SOFTWARE / PROCESS
  execution state
  NOT implemented in this Work Order

A `.pkg` filename alone must NOT make something software.

Do not infer semantics from filename extensions.

Software package identity and metadata must be represented explicitly.


